{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-84199",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{4})+4(\\frac{1}{8})+5(\\frac{1}{16})+6(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+4(\\frac{3}{8})+9(\\frac{1}{4})+16(\\frac{1}{8})+25(\\frac{1}{16})+36(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}-{(\\frac{45}{16})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{155}{16}-\\frac{2025}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{455}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
